  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Higher Education Scholarship Program (HES-2) - LAU</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">(Lebanon):  .In 2025, USAID/Lebanon will support Lebanese students graduating from public and private schools who demonstrate academic merit and high financial need to attend the U.S.-accredited and chartered Lebanese American University (LAU) under the HES-2 program. This activity will fund the studies of at least 45 Lebanese students enrolled in the 2025-2026 academic year. The program will cover full undergraduate tuition, monthly stipends, housing or transportation allowance, books, laptops, and medical insurance for students majoring in academic fields with high prospects for meaningful employment. HES-2 will endeavor to maximize students&apos; potential to contribute to the long-term political, economic, and social development of Lebanon through academic excellence, leadership training, and career preparation. This program is attributed to the higher education earmark (scholarships) and is directed by Congress and will contribute to improved job readiness that will ultimately help students strengthen their income-earning potential. Moreover, the HES-2 program will provide financial aid support to approximately 650 students at LAU who have been adversely affected financially by the deteriorating situation in Lebanon using the Higher Education Economic Crises Directive (HEED) funds. Of the $14 million in HEED directive funds, $7.5 million will be met through this implementing mechanism..</narrative>
  </description>
